Debounce: wait for pause in calls, fire once after quiet gap. Each new call reset timer. Good for search-as-you-type, resize handlers.

Throttle: fire at most once per fixed interval, regardless of call count. Good for scroll handlers, drag events.

```js
function debounce(fn, wait) {
  let t;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(t);
    t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), wait);
  };
}

function throttle(fn, wait) {
  let last = 0;
  return (...args) => {
    const now = Date.now();
    if (now - last >= wait) {
      last = now;
      fn(...args);
    }
  };
}
```
